)</span> <span class=\"fn\">⋯</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Runs the loop `Tail.forInFrom lo hi j₀ hlo () body k` with no variable whose step `j` maps the\narray `a` by `F j.toNat`, before it runs the next step: it maps the array by\n`iterRange F j₀.toNat hi.toNat`, and then runs `k`. This is the case of a loop of loops, where `F j`\nis the model of the inner loop.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int32/Stride.html#ScalarArray.Int32Array.InPlace.Tail.run_forInFrom_unit","kind":"theorem","line":621,"name":"ScalarArray.Int32Array.InPlace.Tail.run_forInFrom_unit","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/7ffd513add11df79848981c4efa28480b0e2e483/ScalarArray/Int32/Stride.lean#L621-L639"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int32/Stride.html#ScalarArray.Int32Array.InPlace.Tail.run_forInFrom\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int32Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">InPlace</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tail</span>.<span class=\"name\">run_forInFrom</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">γ</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">lo </span><span class=\"fn\">hi </span><span class=\"fn\">j₀</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hlo</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">lo</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Da