larArray.Int32Array\">Int32Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">idx</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">lo </span><span class=\"fn\">hi</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">g</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int32\">Int32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int32\">Int32</a></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int32/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int32Array\">Int32Array</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The array `a` with `g i a[idx i]` written at the index `idx i`, for each `i` from `lo` up to\n`hi - 1`, in this order, where `g i` sees the earlier writes. Indices out of bounds are skipped.\nIt is the model of a loop that updates the elements at the indices `idx i`, such as the steps\n`s.idx i` of a stride `s`.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int32/Stride.html#ScalarArray.Int32Array.modifyAt","kind":"def","line":61,"name":"ScalarArray.Int32Array.modifyAt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/7ffd513add11df79848981c4efa28480b0e2e483/ScalarArray/Int32/Stride.lean#L61-L69"}}],"imports":["Init","ScalarArray.Int32.Program","ScalarArray.Internal","ScalarArray.Stride"],"instances":[],"name":"ScalarArray.Int32.Stride"}